Here are the 30 deferred findings -- things that aren't obvious fixes or need design input:
tomd: YAML / front-matter parsing scope (4)

    api.py:_unquote_yaml_scalar -- Only handles \n, ", \\. Other YAML escapes like \t, \x, \u are passed through mangled. But this parser is explicitly scoped to tomd's own emission, which only produces those three escapes. Expanding it risks fixing a problem that never occurs.

    api.py:_parse_front_matter_body -- Discards lines starting with space/tab/- before a key line, so indented YAML continuations are silently lost. Same rationale: only parses the restricted shape tomd emits. General YAML support would require pulling in a real YAML library.

    api.py:_strip_body_metadata_text -- Pipe tables interrupted by blank lines aren't recognized as one table. Fixing requires multi-pass table detection and could remove real content.

    api.py:_strip_toc_replace -- TOCs over 300 lines are preserved. Likely intentional: huge "TOC-shaped" blocks may be real appendix content.

tomd HTML: soup mutation and extraction heuristics (5)

    extract.py:_get_text_br_separated / _parse_mpark_authors -- Mutate the live BeautifulSoup tree by replacing <br> tags. Fixing requires deep-copying the soup or refactoring the extraction pipeline. High regression risk.

    extract.py:_extract_generic_metadata -- Ignores middle columns in wide tables; skips continuation rows unless the current field is reply. These are heuristics tuned to real WG21 paper layouts. Changing without test fixtures from affected papers risks regressions.

    extract.py:_enrich_reply_to -- Pairs bare_names and bare_emails by list position with zip. Wrong ordering yields incorrect pairs. No obviously better algorithm without more context about the HTML structures this encounters.

    extract.py:strip_boilerplate -- Removes all div[data-fill-with], not just known boilerplate. Unclear which Bikeshed-generated divs should be preserved.

    render.py:_render_code_table -- All code blocks emitted as ` cpp . Non-C++ snippets get mislabeled. Possibly intentional for WG21 papers where C++ is the overwhelmingly dominant language.

tomd PDF: geometry and heuristics (8)

    cleanup.py:strip_repeating / cleanup_text -- Block bbox becomes stale after line/span edits. Fixing properly requires propagating geometry updates through the entire pipeline, touching many functions.

    cleanup.py:strip_hidden_blocks -- O(spans x regions) per page. Could use spatial indexing, but current cost is acceptable for typical WG21 papers.

    cleanup.py:find_hidden_regions -- "Black" check only matches 0, (0,0,0), 0x000000. Misses some float RGB encodings. Expanding risks false positives.

    pipeline.py:_run_pipeline -- body_fonts is top 5 by character count. A body font outside that set causes hidden-region heuristics to strip real text. Expanding risks including noise fonts.

    pipeline.py:_get_page0_text_colors -- Later trace entries at the same rounded y overwrite earlier ones. Unclear which color should win for mixed-color lines.

    pipeline.py:_parse_pdf_info_date -- Accepts any 8-digit prefix as a date with no month/day validation. The field is best-effort; rejecting non-standard generator dates would lose data.

    wg21.py:extract_metadata_from_blocks -- Every pre-label title candidate index is added to consumed, risking removal of real body content. Narrowing requires tracking which candidate was actually selected.

    spans.py:_normalize_line_spans -- Single left+right sweep may leave new mid-word boundaries. Multi-pass would be needed but impact is unclear without failing test cases.

tomd PDF: qa.py naming and semantics (3)

    qa.py:unfenced_code_lines -- Actually counts paragraphs, not lines. Renaming the metric would break the JSON schema for existing QA reports. Needs a migration strategy.

    qa.py:_count_mojibake -- Unicode-topic title suppresses U+FFFD counting but still adds ftfy.badness penalty. The two detection paths have different semantics by design; merging risks false negatives.

    render.py:_fix_misnested_blocks -- Re-scans the full tree each iteration until stable. Pathological nesting can be very slow. No obvious fix without rewriting to iterative.

CLI: design decisions (3)

    convert.py:_qa_command -- Exits 0 even when individual papers fail QA. May be intentional: QA is informational, not a gate.

    logutil.py:configure_console_logging -- Early-return guard prevents reconfiguring verbosity in-process. Intentional idempotency for single-process CLI use.

    jobs.py:_papers_from_scope -- "all" path does O(n) resolve_year_for_paper calls. Fixing requires a new batch query method on StorageBackend, which changes the ABC interface.

review pipeline (3)

    pipeline.py:_extract_reads / _extract_tools -- Comma splitting breaks if labels contain commas. Current names never do; adding escaping is overengineering.

web_tools (3)

    brave.py:_TokenBucket.acquire -- Burst capacity equals _rate, so many coroutines can pass nearly back-to-back. Tightening requires understanding Brave's actual rate limit enforcement.

    session.py:WebResearcher.web_search -- Returns [] for both transport failures and genuine empty results. Changing the return type is an API contract change that affects the review pipeline's tool interface.

paperstore: API design (1)

    factory.py:from_uri -- Ignores workspace_dir when file:// has a path. Documented behavior; changing it risks breaking callers that rely on the URI taking precedence.

